            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n \n> 1. Set `cmdheight=0` (e.g., via noice.nvim)\n> \n> 2. Open a vertical split (e.g., neo-tree sidebar)\n> \n> 3. Run `:res 10` to shrink the current window height\n> \n> 4. Observe that `cmdheight` jumps from 0 to ~30 and stays there\n\nThis behavior is observed without enabled 'mini.animate' (even in `nvim --clean`). It is the result of Neovim being able to resize window vertically only by increasing 'cmdheight'. So 'mini.animate' final result seems to be expected, although the resize happens without animation (which I'd accept as a known limitation).",
