            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I need to correct my report — sorry for the confusion.\n\nThe actual issue is not just `:res 10` (shrinking), but the **recovery after shrinking**:\n\n1. `cmdheight=0`, open a horizontal split\n2. `:res 10` — window shrinks (cmdheight stays 0, this is fine with a split)\n3. `:res 1000` — **window does not grow back**\n\nI confirmed that `:res 1000` works correctly in `nvim --clean` but fails with mini.animate loaded. So this does seem to be a mini.animate issue, not a Neovim core behavior.\n\nCould you reopen this? Again, sorry for the inaccurate initial report.",
